{
  "_notes": [
    "Pirates of the Caribbean V6.00, all four sets (potc_600af/ai/as/gf). Upstream had no map for any POTC set.",
    "NVRAM fields were read from the ROM image by backport tools/samrom/samrom.py (adjustment records,",
    "the high-score descriptor table, the Master Volume setter, the score array literal), the rules",
    "validated on the mapped SAM games. The four V6.00 images give identical addresses; V4.00 and",
    "earlier do not and are not claimed.",
    "Free Play is record 33 (ROM adjustment ID 34), Balls Per Game 30, Credit Limit 32: the offset-0 layout.",
    "A saved potc_600as NVRAM from an ALP4K cabinet validates every declared record: the three",
    "adjustments and Master Volume (60, check byte 195) by their check bytes, and all ten champion",
    "records by checksum16 at +28 (32-byte records), including a Grand Champion earned on the cabinet",
    "(CWP, 137,367,130) and the factory high scores below it.",
    "The five mode champions hold counts, not scores: their factory values are 25 (Pirate King) and",
    "15, 10, 5, 5, so they are declared as counter. The ROM names them PIRATE KING, GAUNTLET CHAMP 1-3",
    "and DAVY JONES CHAMPION, with adjustments 74-78 (PIRATE KING, GAUNTLET CHAMPION 1-3) beside them.",
    "current_player and current_ball are adjacent at 0x00032694/0x00032695, the only candidate the",
    "ROM offers and the only one a headless libpinmame run (two players, two tilts) found.",
    "Status byte 0x000326C0 (player + 0x2C, as on fg_1200af and wpt_140a): 01 in attract, 12 with a",
    "ball in play, 43 while a ball is held, 14 from each tilt to the next ball. game_over is any",
    "value of 0 or 1 (mask 0xFE inverted); tilted is an enum over mask 0x1F with only 20 (0x14) true,",
    "as on wpt_140a, where bit 0x04 also appears in play.",
    "Scores are 4 bytes on 8-byte centres from 0x021109E4.",
    "Master Volume 0x0211024C, 0-63, factory 40, complement check byte after it."
  ],
